# Timiva Mobile Rules

## Purpose

These rules define mobile behavior for Timiva.

## Mobile-first

Timiva is mobile-first. Cursor must prioritize:

```text
Mobile portrait
Mobile landscape
Desktop
```

Desktop is important, but mobile usability is the core experience.

## Mobile portrait

Cursor must ensure:

```text
Main result is visible
CTA is clear
Touch targets are comfortable
Inputs do not overflow
Bottom Control does not hide required content
Bottom Sheet can open and close
Footer does not feel detached
```

## Mobile landscape

Mobile landscape must be tested separately.

Do not assume portrait works means landscape works.

Cursor must check:

```text
Main result remains visible
Inputs do not overflow
Long text does not break layout
Bottom Sheet is not too tall
Bottom Control does not collide with Footer
Returning to portrait restores layout
Ads do not compress the main tool
```

## Bottom Sheet

Bottom Sheet must:

```text
Open and close reliably
Allow background click to close
Avoid ads
Avoid long SEO content
Avoid hiding essential results
Allow inner scroll when content is long
```

## Block conditions

Block if:

```text
Mobile main task cannot be completed
Main result is hidden
Inputs overflow
Bottom Sheet cannot close
Landscape layout is severely broken
```
